# A number with its measurement uncertainty. `10 ± 0.1` and
# the concise `10.5(3)` of the physical tables, where the digits in brackets
# are the uncertainty in the last places, make the same kind of value. It
# propagates through arithmetic, powers and the math functions to first
# order, treating its operands as independent, and is shown in the concise
# form with the uncertainty to two digits.

sheet Literals

| Name        | Value               |
| ----------- | ------------------- |
| plus-minus  | = 10 ± 0.1          |
| expression  | = 10 ± 0.1 * 2      |
| concise     | = 10.5(3)           |
| whole       | = 10(3)             |
| long digits | = 1.5(11)           |
| exact       | = 10.5(0)           |
| fine-structure | = 7.297_352_5643(11)e-3 |

sheet Arithmetic

| Name           | Value                           |
| -------------- | ------------------------------- |
| sum            | = (10 ± 1) + (20 ± 2)           |
| product        | = (100 ± 2) * (0.2 ± 0.01)      |
| quotient       | = (100 ± 2) / (50 ± 1)          |
| exact operand  | = (10 ± 0.1) * 2                |
| power          | = (3 ± 0.1) ** 2                |
| independent    | = (10 ± 1) - (10 ± 1)           |
| sine           | = sin(0.5 ± 0.01)               |
| logarithm      | = ln(100 ± 1)                   |
| root           | = sqrt(4 ± 0.4)                 |
| exact function | = sin(0.5)                      |
| beside Complex | = (10 ± 1) + 3i                 |
| larger than the value | = 0.5 ± 0.8              |
| coarse         | = 1000 ± 200                    |

